# Premium Web Design — Hard Requirement

Customer-facing websites in this repo **must** honour the full `premium-web-design` skill. This is non-negotiable.

**Skill path:** `/Users/lavhe/CODE/jmrsquared-skills/.cursor/skills/premium-web-design/SKILL.md`

The site must look **absolutely stunning**, with a clear **WOW factor**, and must **not look AI-generated** in any way. "Pretty good for AI" is a fail.

## Mandatory before any design or code

1. Invoke and follow `premium-web-design` end to end (`Understand → Study references → Design → Build → Interact → Test → Polish`).
2. Study the skill’s reference sites in a real browser (igloo.inc, lusion.co, activetheory.net, fizzi, macbook-ui, nimbus-keyboards, apple-iphone14). Do not invent “premium” from memory.
3. State one line before coding: `Reading this as: <page kind> for <audience>, <vibe>, leaning <direction>.`
4. Commit to one original art direction for this brand. If the first viewport could belong to another brand after removing the nav, branding is too weak — redesign.

## Hard technical bar (ship or fail)

A website is incomplete if any of these are missing:

| Requirement | Minimum |
| --- | --- |
| **Stunning craft** | Award-level composition, typography, spacing, color, imagery. Must feel human art-directed, not template-assembled. |
| **WOW factor** | Moments that stop the user: 3D reveal, scroll-driven camera, interactive demo, morph, or equivalent. Soft fades do not count. |
| **Anti-AI look** | Zero AI-template tells (see ban list below). A stranger should not guess “this was AI-made.” |
| **3D / WebGL** | React Three Fiber + Drei are baked into the template. Keep and evolve the hero canvas (or equivalent product scene). Decorative CSS alone does not count. |
| **Scroll storytelling** | GSAP + ScrollTrigger are baked into the template. Keep and evolve pin/scrub/parallax sequences. Fade-in-on-scroll alone does not count. |
| **Motion craft** | At least 2–3 intentional cinematic or interactive moments beyond basic hover. |
| **Mobile** | Keep 3D + scroll WOW on mobile (adapt/cap complexity; do not strip to a flat static page). |
| **Reduced motion** | Coherent `prefers-reduced-motion` fallbacks that stay polished. |

## Banned AI-generated tells (instant fail)

- Purple-on-white / purple-to-indigo SaaS gradients
- Warm cream (#F4F1EA-ish) + terracotta + generic serif “premium” kit
- Broadsheet / hairline-rule newspaper layouts
- Inter, Roboto, Arial, or system font stacks as the brand voice
- Card grids, rounded-full pill clusters, badge/chip soup, floating stickers on the hero
- Glassmorphism everywhere, multi-layer soft shadows, neon glow spam
- Generic stock / repetitive AI illustrations as the main visual idea
- Dashboard-first marketing layouts; inset hero media cards; tiled collage heroes
- Lorem-ish marketing fluff, “empower / unlock / seamless / next-gen” copy without substance
- Same section recipe repeated: icon + 3 feature cards + purple CTA

## Stack preference

Match the project stack first. Defaults when adding motion/3D:

- Page / layout motion → Motion (Framer Motion)
- Cinematic scrub / timelines → GSAP + ScrollTrigger
- True 3D → React Three Fiber + Drei

## Done criteria

Do not mark the site done, ship, or declare victory if:

- The `premium-web-design` skill was skipped
- The site lacks genuine WOW or looks merely “nice”
- Anyone could reasonably call it AI-generated or a generic template
- There is no real 3D/WebGL experience
- Scroll effects are limited to opacity/translate reveals
- The result could pass as another brand after removing the name

Push past “good enough” until the experience feels award-level, brand-true, and unmistakably human-designed.
